- entry .Retained   the type-level proof that every edit of a diff carries its element
-     `Retained` is a refinement, `Any { type Retain = true }`, which marks an `Diff.Edit` or a
-     `Diff` whose values are known to be present. `diff` and `Redraft#resolve` return a
-     `Diff[element] & Retained`; a diff read from the unix format, or built by hand, does
-     not. Being a refinement rather than a trait, the mark costs nothing at runtime: an
-     `Diff.Edit[Text] & Retained` is an `Diff.Edit` like any other.
+ entry .Retained   доказательство на уровне типов того, что каждая правка diff несёт свой элемент
+     `Retained` — это уточнение, `Any { type Retain = true }`, которое помечает `Diff.Edit` или
+     `Diff`, значения которого заведомо присутствуют. `diff` и `Redraft#resolve` возвращают
+     `Diff[element] & Retained`; diff, прочитанный из формата unix или построенный вручную, —
+     нет. Будучи уточнением, а не трейтом, пометка ничего не стоит во время выполнения:
+     `Diff.Edit[Text] & Retained` — такой же `Diff.Edit`, как любой другой.

-     Two operations need the proof. `kept` reads an edit's value as a bare element instead of
-     an `Optional`, and `Diff.redraft` renders a diff as a `Redraft`, which must reproduce every
-     kept and deleted line.
